      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name}: Okay, Kung.\nI will have to apologize for the intent of my feedback. This thread was based off of 'what can we do to push the limits of this new feature', and on first impression. However, in posting this, it seems I have ignored the main reason why this was implemented in the first place -- accessibility. I will have to focus on feedback regarding accessibility, and that alone.\nWith that being said, please disregard this thread in particular. However, the last sentence provides a suggestion regarding rotating the main menu, so if one was laying on their side, and their head was tilted sideways, the MM would follow. Should this be a separate thread, so that this one can be closed out?\nThank you. You're doing excellent work.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
